--- body ---
## Context

Rung 4 of the ladder, required before every live install, release or not
(author, 2026-09-23: "my data = caution"). The author's data directory is
46 GB on btrfs, so a reflink copy (`cp -a --reflink=always`) is near-instant
and shares blocks until written. It is the wildest library there is: the 3 853
packless PDFs (0728), the AR6 stall (0793) and both disappearances happened
there.

## Actions

1. A recipe that copies the data directory with Zotero closed, so the SQLite
   files are consistent, and refuses when Zotero is running.
2. Run the sitter on the copy in a clean-room profile until the census settles,
   with the integrity check (0816) against the copy's own before-snapshot.
3. Record the verdict under `verification/acceptance/`.
4. The same recipe takes the pre-install snapshot for rung 5.

## Exit criteria

One recorded clone-rung run on the author's copy, integrity green, and the
copy removed afterwards — or kept with a line naming when it goes.
